Understanding Cloud & AWS Architecture — Simplified! ☁️🔍

quick guide to Cloud & AWS fundamentals:


🔹 1. Cloud Deployment Models

🌐 Public, Private, Hybrid, Multi-Cloud
→ Choose based on security, scalability, and control.


🔹 2. Cloud Service Models

🛠️ IaaS, PaaS, SaaS
→ From managing VMs (IaaS) to deploying apps without managing infra (PaaS), and consuming ready apps (SaaS) — know when to use what.


🔹 3. Workload Mapping

📊 Match the right workload to the right environment
→ Consider compute, memory, latency, and compliance needs.


🔹 4. Anycast vs. GeoDNS

🌍 Speed vs. Strategy
→ Anycast = nearest route for faster delivery (low latency)
→ GeoDNS = location-based routing (regional content/compliance)


🔹 5. EC2 Sizing

📏 Right-size to optimize cost + performance
→ Use AWS Compute Optimizer or CloudWatch metrics. Don’t overpay for underused resources!


🔹 6. CapEx vs. OpEx

💰 Cloud flips the finance model
→ Traditional = CapEx (buy servers)
→ Cloud = OpEx (pay-as-you-go) — agile, scalable, and budget-friendly!


🎯 Cloud isn’t just tech — it’s strategy, performance, and smart investment.
